    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nIf there are no actions or external changes to apply, then `synchronize` should return `false` since nothing has been changed/synchronized.\n\nThis would make it trivial to implement a `sync_or_goto` action:\n\n```lua\nfunction sync_or_goto() if not MiniFiles.synchronize() then MiniFiles.go_in() end end\n```",
