    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> If there are no actions or external changes to apply, then `synchronize` should return `false` since nothing has been changed/synchronized.\n\nI don't think this interpretation is universally useful. The case of \"no actions to apply\" seems closer to \"successful\" sync, then not. It *did* successfully synchronize the state of explorer to the state of file system; it just so happened that there was nothing to do here.\n\nThe return value was added for the use case described in #1439: \"... rewrite 'l' map on file to synchronize, then open the file if changes to the file system were accepted.\". I.e. \"sync *and* goto\", which is feels more appropriate of a mapping (although I'd discourage even that in favor of explicit `=` to sync).\n\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2025-05-21T07:52:34Z",
